FP8 KV cache on sm_8x, applied after sm86-tune.diff (patch -p1 --fuzz=0). Only --kv-cache-dtype fp8 takes it.

The image accepts fp8 KV on SM12x only: its attention kernels convert E4M3 with `cvt` instructions that need
sm_89+, and Triton has no fp8 pointer type below that. Here the cache is passed as bytes: the attention
prologue (ops/sconv.py) encodes unit-scale E4M3 in integer maths (round to nearest even, saturating at 448, the
same byte `cvt.rn.satfinite.e4m3x2.f32` gives), and the attention kernel (ops/attention_sm90.py) decodes
exactly with a shift into an fp32 word and a 2**120 scale. The image's own attention kernel and the tuning's
Ampere paths stay as they are; bf16 runs do not reach any changed line.

The conv-state manager of sm86-tune.diff assumes prefix hits on `block_size` tokens. With an fp8 target cache
next to the bf16 DSpark draft cache, the attention pages hold 128 tokens and hits land on 128, so its tail is
sized for that (sconv_swa_attn.py).

Measured on 2x RTX 3090: NOTES.md, "FP8 KV cache".

